d":null,"_gate_int_coverage":null,"_gp_int_coverage":null,"_score_int_coverage":null,"_gate_net_debt_ebitda":null,"_gp_net_debt_ebitda":null,"_score_net_debt_ebitda":null,"_gate_accruals":-0.010839468463349733,"_gp_accruals":true,"_score_accruals":65.8,"_gate_rev_volatility":0.1045793841685855,"_gp_rev_volatility":true,"_score_rev_volatility":84.4,"_gate_margin_vs_hist":0.04445940322324933,"_gp_margin_vs_hist":true,"_score_margin_vs_hist":44.4,"_gate_piotroski":5,"_gp_piotroski":false,"_score_piotroski":55.6,"_gate_spread":null,"_gp_spread":null,"_score_spread":null,"_gate_roic_consistency":null,"_gp_roic_consistency":null,"_score_roic_consistency":null,"_gate_incr_roic":null,"_gp_incr_roic":null,"_score_incr_roic":null,"_gate_margin_advantage":null,"_gp_margin_advantage":null,"_score_margin_advantage":null,"_gate_pool_share":-0.06489816772594259,"_gp_pool_share":false,"_score_pool_share":14.0,"_gate_rev_durability":0.058425905015821344,"_gp_rev_durability":true,"_score_rev_durability":54.2,"_gate_fcf_durability":null,"_gp_fcf_durability":null,"_score_fcf_durability":null,"_gate_margins":null,"_gp_margins":null,"_score_margins":null,"_gate_fund_growth":null,"_gp_fund_growth":null,"_score_fund_growth":null,"_gate_shrhldr_yield":0.01191442960475432,"_gp_shrhldr_yield":false,"_score_shrhldr_yield":24.3,"_gate_share_shrink":-0.03640543269876051,"_gp_share_shrink":true,"_score_share_shrink":95.5,"_gate_sbc_dilution":0.019660319973920544,"_gp_sbc_dilution":true,"_score_sbc_dilution":67.2,"_gate_insider_own":0.42341998,"_gp_insider_own":true,"_score_insider_own":100.0,"_gate_insider_buying":null,"_gp_insider_buying":null,"_score_insider_buying":null,"pf":[],"description_full":"Oppenheimer Holdings Inc. operates as a middle-market investment bank and full-service broker-dealer. It provides brokerage services covering corporate equity and debt securities, money market instruments, exchange-traded options, municipal bonds, mutual funds, exchange-traded funds, certain precious metals, and unit investment trusts; financial and wealth planning services; and margin lending services. The company also offers asset management services, including separately managed accounts, mutual fund managed accounts, discretionary portfolio management programs, non-discretionary investment advisory and consultation services, alternative investments, portfolio enhancement programs, and institutional taxable fixed income portfolio management strategies and solutions, as well as taxable and non-taxable fixed income portfolios and strategies. In addition, it provides investment banking services, such as strategic advisory services and capital markets products; merger and acquisition, equities capital market, debt capital market, debt advisory and restructuring, and fund placement services; and institutional equity sales and trading, equity research, equity derivatives and index options, convertible bonds, event driven sales and trading, and portfolio and electronic trading, as well as provides custody, clearing, and prime services. Further, the company offers institutional fixed income sales and trading, fixed income research, public finance, and municipal trading services; and proprietary trading and investment activities. Additionally, it provides underwriting, market-making, trust, and discount services, as well as a cloud-based financial market. The company serves high-net-worth individuals and families, corporate executives, public and private businesses, institutions and corporations, governments, financial sponsors, and domestic and international investors. The company was founded in 1881 and is headquartered in New York, New York.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Robert Steven Lowenthal | CEO, President & Director | Age 49 | Compensation: $8.5M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 3K people. Revenue per employee of $544K ranks in the above the sector median among Financial Services peers. Each employee generates $61K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $11K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 16\u00d7 revenue per employee (reasonable relative to workforce productivity).","financial_summary":["Oppenheimer Holdings, Inc. is a small-cap financial services business with a $886M market cap on $1.6B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +14% over the past three years and +6% annually across the full decade, the kind of sustained demand persistence that marks a compounder.","Returns on capital run at 8% against a 10% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests.","The business throws off $184M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 11 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 1.27\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, the balance sheet carries net cash, which is the gold standard: the business never has to make desperate decisions in a bad year, and thin 2.4\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Shareholder yield is only 1.2%, a thin return of capital, and insiders hold 42% of the shares, so management thinks like owners because it is one \u2014 the strongest alignment there is, and profit capture is only 0.5\u00d7 the fair share, suggesting no structural edge inside its industry."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (1.2) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Low reinvestment-driven growth suggests the compounding engine has stalled","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Operating margins 16% below sector median \u2014 a cost disadvantage the moat cannot hide","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Priced near or above estimated fair value, so the margin of safety has been bid away","sev":"amber","cat":"valuation","magnitude":0.007178243248736662},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"High market volatility with VIX at 36, signaling elevated fear","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Widening credit spreads suggest growing stress in corporate debt markets","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Broad market in a downtrend, trading below its 200-day average","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Interest rate regime shifts \u2014 a rapid move in rates can invert the yield curve, crush bond portfolios, and trigger deposit flight simultaneously.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["30 consecutive years of dividend payments \u2014 an operating record that makes the dividend claim credible","Healthy payout ratio leaves room for both dividend growth and reinvestment","Minimal goodwill on the balance sheet \u2014 low impairment risk"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Unusual Machines Drops 11% Despite Oppenheimer\u2019s $30 Target; Ondas Retreats 7%, Red Cat Falls 4%","source":"247wallst.com","link":"https://247wallst.com/investing/2026/11/20/unusual-machines-drops-11-despite-oppenheimers-30-target-ondas-retreats-7-red-cat-falls-4/","date":"2026-11-20","timestamp":1795190176.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":-0.103,"tier":1,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"DigitalOcean (DOCN) Stock Fair Value Edges Lower After Mixed Analyst Views On Q3","source":"finance.yahoo.com","link":"https://finance.yahoo.com/markets/stocks/articles/digitalocean-docn-stock-fair-value-201154223.html","date":"2026-11-20","timestamp":1795205514.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.883,"tier":2,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"CAPR Stock Gains Ahead Of Weekend FDA Deramiocel Decision After Rough Week","source":"finance.yahoo.com","link":"https://finance.yahoo.com/healthcare/articles/capr-stock-gains-ahead-weekend-200531177.html","date":"2026-11-2